TITLE:: OndaDef
summary:: Onda definition manager
categories:: UGens>Onda
related:: Classes/Onda, Classes/ControlSpec, Classes/NamedControl

DESCRIPTION::
OndaDef is the language-side owner of a compiled Onda definition. It associates a link::Classes/Symbol:: key with inline Onda source, an Onda source file, or an Onda project, and asks the link::Classes/Server:: plugin to compile it for the server's current sample rate and block size.

OndaDef is not a link::Classes/UGen:: and does not process audio. After a successful compile it caches the SC-facing input and output metadata, registers itself by key, and can be passed directly to one or more link::Classes/Onda:: UGens. Onda can alternatively retrieve the current registered definition from its link::Classes/Symbol:: key. Sending another definition with the same key replaces the compiled server program and hot-swaps compatible running Onda UGens.

Compilation is asynchronous. Use the action callback to create synths or perform work that depends on the compiled definition:

code::
OndaDef(\name, sourceOrPath).send(s, { |definition|
    { Onda.ar(definition) }.play;
});
::

An inline source string is written to a temporary code::.onda:: file before compilation. Use a code::.onda::/code::.on:: path when the program has relative source dependencies, and use an code::.ondaproject:: manifest for project-relative sources and buffer assets.

SUBSECTION:: Definition lifetime

Definitions live in the server plugin and must be sent after the server boots. A successful replacement under the same key reinitializes every attached Onda UGen. A failed compile leaves the previously published server program running. Calling code::free:: unloads the server definition; attached Onda UGens then output silence.

SUBSECTION:: Cached metadata

After compilation, link::Classes/OndaDef#-ins:: contains the ordered SC endpoint descriptors used by Onda. Each descriptor contains code::name::, code::rate::, and code::meta::. The metadata contains the endpoint code::kind:: and, when available, its code::init:: value. Ranged params also contain code::spec::, the same link::Classes/ControlSpec:: stored by name in link::Classes/OndaDef#-specs::. link::Classes/OndaDef#-outs:: is the flattened number of audio output channels.

The generated specs preserve the Onda range, linear/logarithmic scale or curve, unit, step grid, and default. OndaDef does not register them globally or attach them to SynthDef controls. Use one explicitly when a control should carry that metadata:

code::
var cutoff = \cutoff.kr(spec: definition.specs[\cutoff]);
Onda.ar(definition, (cutoff: cutoff));
::

The control and Onda UGen still exchange plain values; link::Classes/ControlSpec#-map:: and GUI widgets perform normalized mapping when requested.

SUBSECTION:: Current limitations

list::
## Onda teletype::ins::, teletype::params::, and teletype::events:: must be scalar.
## teletype::ins:: must use teletype::f32::; teletype::params:: may use any scalar primitive type.
## teletype::events:: must use a single scalar primitive payload and fire whenever their control value changes.
## teletype::outs:: must use teletype::f32:: endpoint types (teletype::f32:: or teletype::f32[N]::).
## SC link::Classes/Buffer:: overrides must be teletype::buffer<f32...>:: and are driven from control-rate code::bufnum:: inputs. Project-owned buffers may use any Onda primitive element type.
## Project-owned buffers with non-teletype::f32:: elements are omitted from teletype::ins:: and cannot be overridden from SuperCollider.
## Buffer arrays require an code::.ondaproject::, are omitted from teletype::ins::, and cannot be overridden from SuperCollider.
## Onda teletype::print(...):: output and top-level delegate occurrences are written to the link::Classes/Server:: log rather than delivered to sclang. Capture and formatting storage are bounded per Onda UGen.
## A hot-swap must retain a compatible SC input interface and flattened output channel count. Relaunch link::Classes/Synth:: instances after changing the interface shape.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create an uncompiled Onda definition. Call code::send:: after the target Server has booted.
ARGUMENT:: key
A link::Classes/Symbol:: used to register and later retrieve the definition.
ARGUMENT:: source
A link::Classes/String:: containing inline Onda source, a code::.onda::/code::.on:: file path, or a code::.ondaproject:: manifest path.

METHOD:: free
Free the definition registered under a key from the default Server.
ARGUMENT:: key
The definition's link::Classes/Symbol:: key.

METHOD:: freeAll
Free all registered definitions from the default Server and clear the language-side registry.

METHOD:: all
The link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: of successfully compiled definitions, indexed by key.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: send
Asynchronously compile and publish the definition on a Server. On success, metadata is cached, the definition is registered in code::OndaDef.all::, compatible running Onda UGens are hot-swapped, and the action is evaluated.
ARGUMENT:: server
Target link::Classes/Server::. Defaults to code::Server.default::.
ARGUMENT:: action
Optional link::Classes/Function:: evaluated after successful compilation with this OndaDef as its argument. It is not evaluated on failure.

METHOD:: add
Alias for code::send::.

METHOD:: free
Unload this definition from a Server and remove it from the language-side registry. Running Onda UGens attached to it become silent.
ARGUMENT:: server
Target link::Classes/Server::. Defaults to code::Server.default::.

METHOD:: query
Post the key, definition id, generation, cached input descriptors, flattened output count, and parameter specs.

METHOD:: key
The definition's registration key.

METHOD:: id
Server definition id retained for this key for the lifetime of the sclang process.

METHOD:: generation
Latest compile/free generation sent for this definition key. Generations prevent stale asynchronous compiles from replacing newer requests.

METHOD:: source
The inline Onda source or resolved source/project path supplied at construction.

METHOD:: ins
Ordered SC endpoint metadata populated after a successful compile. This includes Onda inputs, params, events, and overridable buffers; project-only endpoints such as buffer arrays and non-teletype::f32:: buffers are omitted.

METHOD:: specs
A link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: mapping each ranged param name to its generated link::Classes/ControlSpec::. Unranged params and other endpoint kinds are omitted. Specs are populated after successful compilation and are never registered or attached automatically.

METHOD:: outs
Flattened audio output channel count populated after a successful compile.

EXAMPLES::

code::
(
s.waitForBoot {
	var code = "
params:
  freq = 220.0 {20.0, 20000.0}

init:
  phase = 0.0

block:
  incr = freq / SR
  sample:
    out1 = sin(TWO_PI * phase)
    phase = wrap(phase + incr, 0.0, 1.0)
";

    OndaDef(\sine, code).send(s, { |definition|
        { Onda.ar(definition, MouseX.kr(200, 1000, 1)).dup }.play;
    });
};
)

::
